00:29:00.380 --> 00:29:15.280
Tanner, Bertrand: 9 microns, so in the longer sarcomere length is in black, and the shorter sarcomere length is in white. And you can see that you get sort of a similar response, but there's some shifts to it. And these shifts in the dips and the humps

147
00:29:15.510 --> 00:29:23.340
Tanner, Bertrand: And how those change, vertically have to do with cross-bridge binding, and how those change horizontally have to do with the crossbridge kinetics.

148
00:29:23.740 --> 00:29:29.089
Tanner, Bertrand: And so… We take these data and we fit it to a model.

